+# Causal GDN prefill reference targeting R4D M1
+
+The chunked prefill path can make an earlier prefix depend on future gates and
+on chunk partitioning through cumulative-gate reconstruction, midpoint scaling
+and the whole-call extreme-decay fallback. This experimental reference computes
+raw gates and follows a token-ordered recurrence instead.
+
+**This reference targets the existing unfused R4D M1 arithmetic.** It preserves
+that path's FP32 beta and output rounding rule. It is distinct from the later
+stock-FLA contract used by the final compiled 10K experiment. Neither result is
+silently treated as proof of the other numerical target.
+
+```text
+experimental/causal_gdn_prefill/
+├── raw_convolution.hip       # raw QKV and per-token gates from the pinned producer
+├── gdn_causal_prefill.hip    # ordered recurrence; optional prepared FP32 Q/K
+├── candidate.hip            # combined translation unit
+├── build.py                 # source-bound current-header CPU compilation
+├── BUILD_INPUTS.json
+├── build_gdn_causal_prefill.py # preserved original build and source contract
+├── probe_gdn_causal_prefill.py # preserved native partition/state probe
+└── SOURCE_PROVENANCE.json
+```
+
+Build from the repository root, with ROCm installed:
+
+```sh
+uv run --no-project python experimental/causal_gdn_prefill/build.py \
+  --output /tmp/r4d-causal-prefill
+```
+
+This emits a library, compiler log and `BUILT_UNTESTED` receipt into a new
+directory, without running the GPU. The original builder and native probe need
+the pinned Radiance support environment and authenticated synthetic capture.
+The producer source and GDN helper header still match their original hashes;
+the current `r4d.h` does not. A current-header build requires fresh ABI and native
+qualification before use. This experiment is not installed in the public API.
+
+For a previous state S, per-token gate g and beta, the recurrence is:
+
+```text
+D = exp(g) * S
+p = D * k
+u = beta * (v - p)
+S_next = D + u * transpose(k)
+o = S_next * q
+```
+
+The actual source fixes the finite-precision order, normalization and casts;
+real-number equations alone do not specify them. Every step consumes only the
+current token and previous state. An empty chunk is identity. If each call
+implements that same finite transition F and preserves its state, partition
+independence follows by composition of F. This is a scoped structural argument,
+not a proof of the compiled GPU binary for all inputs.
+
+The pinned optimized reference passed **52/52** native comparisons across two
+synthetic layers, including complete partitions, causal prefixes, future-gate
+changes, nonzero state/history, strided gates and empty sequences. Prepared-Q/K
+plus recurrence took 2.380/2.373 ms in those two 2,049-token layer controls.
+Those are operator timings, not decode throughput. A whole-model diagnostic made
+initial prefill exact while preserving evidence of the then-unfixed decode
+discrepancies. The later stock-contract repair is published separately in
+[Radiance #11](https://github.com/magiccodingman/vllm-radiance/pull/11).
+
+[Investigation report](https://github.com/Terrydaktal/qwen-r9700-lab/releases/tag/d7-report-v1.0.0).
